  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+2 & =0 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =-2 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =-0.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(-0.4)=-21.8014{\u2026}^{\u2218}\u2248-{22.80}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSince $-{22.80}^{\u2218}$ lies outside the domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={180}^{\u2218}+(-{21.80}^{\u2218})\u2248{158.20}^{\u2218},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={360}^{\u2218}+(-{21.80}^{\u2218})\u2248{338.20}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are $x={158}^{\u2218}$ and $x={338}^{\u2218}.$",
